expr main <([I, we, you, he, she, they] herd [(a noise), (a sound), (a voice), (the noise), (the sound), (the news), (a rumor), (that), (about), (from), (nothing), (something), (anything), (someone), (it)]), (herd)>

let message "Did you mean `heard`?"
let description "A `herd` is a group of animals; `heard` is the past tense of `hear`."
let kind "Spelling"
let becomes "heard"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "I herd a noise." "I heard a noise."
test "I herd a sound." "I heard a sound."
test "I herd a voice." "I heard a voice."
test "I herd the news." "I heard the news."
test "I herd a rumor." "I heard a rumor."
test "I herd that." "I heard that."
test "I herd nothing." "I heard nothing."
test "I herd something." "I heard something."
test "I herd someone." "I heard someone."
test "I herd from them." "I heard from them."
test "We herd the noise." "We heard the noise."
test "She herd about it." "She heard about it."
test "They herd a sound." "They heard a sound."
test "He herd that story." "He heard that story."
test "You herd the news." "You heard the news."

allows "A herd of cattle crossed."
allows "I heard a noise."
allows "They herd the sheep."
allows "We herd the cattle home."
allows "The herd moved on."
allows "She heard the news."
